  "scientific_review": [
    "All four original January 15/July 15, 2022 regional cases retain all 28 original section anchors, exact source positions, primary depths, paired model spans, source pointers, native selection status, frames, scopes and gates. Unselected, edge/support-edge and censored primary nodes remain explicit. Source arrays and diagnostics stay immutable behind pinned facts, source review, manifest and correctly oriented transport ledger.",
    "Both targets use fixed 0-degree northward components, primary 10 cm/s, surface >5 cm/s and complete finite upper-200-m signed-integral support. Native western index breaks ties. Shallow support exclusion, broad-gate contamination and geographic component orientation limit representativeness. No independent velocity axis, water-mass boundary, isobath or flow-normal full width is established.",
    "Irminger 56–65 N scope is partial western Reykjanes Ridge upper-branch geography. Fresh source text describes two surface-intensified cores, intermediate southward return and deeper northward water. A selected local maximum can switch cores and is not their sum or one coherently tracked core. Connected velocity support does not separate mode water from deep water masses. Greenland return, North Icelandic continuation, interior gyre, opposite ridge-side flow and detached eddies remain distinct targets and contamination risks.",
    "West Spitsbergen 73–79.6 N scope is partial northward slope-current geography, including the original 77.25 N section. Front Current, recirculation, Barents inflow, shelf/fjord exchange and downstream branches remain separate targets. Spitsbergen Atlantic naming is not merged. No Atlantic Water thermal/salinity screen is applied. Source conservative-temperature/Absolute-Salinity criteria are not transferred to HYCOM in-situ temperature or practical salinity.",
    "The glider archive is a validation lead, not a depth-resolved observed velocity input to this batch. Dundas and Fer (2026) combine hydrographic shear with satellite reference and replace anomalous DAC consistently. No archive fields, satellite fields or author velocity reconstruction are acquired here. The 1,000-m sampling limit, 20–500-m average and selected width statistic are not a current bottom, annual range or matched width-depth area.",
    "Frozen v18 source-to-reference and v12 adjacent-only interpolation keep every original section and gap. Only adjacent eligible anchors support assumed interpolation. A no-selection source has explicit unsampled gate-midpoint geometry without depth/profile claims. No weaker interior substitution, cutoff filling, gap skipping, extrapolation or forced seasonal continuity occurs. Reference connectors are not admitted measured current lengths.",
    "All 80 earlier supported scenarios, historical unresolved cases, all previous CSV cells and canonical ownership lists are preserved by cloud checks. Immutable v14 base and nine earlier addenda remain byte-pinned. Inventory v10 adds one pinned addendum/CSV without rewriting old data or expanding a full JSON snapshot. No publication or field-processing caps increase.",
    "Eleven cloud projection tests check original cases/anchors, source values/positions/pointers, frames/gates/scopes, selection and depth censoring gaps, unsampled geometry, adjacent interpolation, mutation rejection, piece/input integrity, counts and earlier cases/CSV cells/ownership. The actual-latitude transport ledger is pinned. Six canonical baseline tests passed on the same exact code commit. Calculations and tests ran sequentially in the cloud on one idle CPU; local work was metadata/code/hash review and exact artifact retention.",
    "Two snapshots do not establish monthly means, annual extrema, seasonal envelopes, confidence intervals or independent observations. Model threshold spans remain qualified regional estimates, not physical whole-current thickness or water-mass boundaries. No complete physical route depth, matched section area, physical current volume, state join or global total is admitted. Broader coverage, observational/seasonal validation and runtime/query integration remain unfinished."
  ],
